{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.7,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "obs": "On the EPD_Driver sheet, C1 is populated as 0.1 µF / 16 V, whereas every other cap in the same group (C5, C7, C8, C9, C10) is 1 µF / 25 V.",
      "exp": "The specification's component table maps the PDI reference C2 (default 1 µF / 25 V) to schematic C1, i.e. C1 is intended to be 1 µF / 25 V.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EPD_Driver.kicad_sch: C1 value reads '0.1uF/16V' (next to C2 '1uF/6.3V')"}
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD boost/charge-pump decoupling capacitor is 10× too small and its voltage rating is below the intended 25 V, so input filtering of the e-paper power stage is inadequate; this can cause boost-converter instability, display artifacts, and possible over-voltage stress on the cap.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    },
    {
      "category": "polarity",
      "components": ["U6", "U7"],
      "pins": ["U6.1", "U6.2", "U7.1"],
      "nets": ["BAT+", "Net-(U6-A)"],
      "obs": "On the EthernetAndPower sheet the battery holder U7 sits to the right of U6 while the global label BAT+ is tied to U6 pin 1 (the anode); U6 pin 2 (cathode) connects to U7 pin 1 (+). Thus anode = BAT+ and cathode = battery.",
      "exp": "The specification requires U6's anode on the battery side (via U7) and its cathode on BAT+, so the diode blocks USB/adapter 5 V from back-feeding the cell and lets the cell feed BAT+.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Battery (U7, 18650 holder) → pin 1 → Net-(U6-A) → U6 (SS2040FL) anode→cathode → BAT+"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "U6 SS2040FL ... netlist: anode on battery (via U7), cathode on BAT+"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EthernetAndPower.kicad_sch: U6 (SS2040FL) with global labels 'BAT+'/'BAT-' on its left (anode) side and U7 1043 on its right (cathode) side"}
      ],
      "impact": "With the isolation diode reversed, the 18650 cannot power BAT+ (board dead on battery), and any USB/DC-barrel source on BAT+ forward-biases U6 and dumps current into the raw cell — the exact fault the diode was meant to prevent.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Two deviations from the reference design are visible: C1 on the EPD_Driver sheet is 0.1 µF/16 V instead of the specified 1 µF/25 V, and on the EthernetAndPower sheet the battery-isolation diode U6 appears wired in reverse (anode to BAT+, cathode to the cell). The C1 value/rating mismatch is the higher-confidence finding."
}

